za in 2007.\n\n**UN Aid Efforts**\n\nThe UN aid agency for Palestinian refugees has opened 80 of its schools to more than 200,000 Palestinians fleeing the violence. The agency's chief, Pierre Kraehenbuehl, has said that Israel must try harder to ensure that civilians are not hurt, especially in Gaza, where 1.7 million people are squeezed into a small coastal territory.\n\n**Regional Response**\n\nThe conflict has also had a regional impact, with protests and demonstrations taking place in cities around the world. In Paris, hundreds of riot police were deployed near",
